//? Title: Simulation ranking, budget allocation and racing
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

> Ranking, allocation and finite-list racing

Kim–Nelson estimates the variance of paired differences in the pilot
and screens on a shrinking indifference-zone boundary. OCBA directs the
next simulation toward candidates whose empirical allocation is below
a target derived from gaps and variances. Confidence-bound racing uses
bounded observations and a time-uniform error allocation across rounds.
Friedman racing screens on within-block ranks, then uses a post-hoc
comparison with the leading mean rank.

See [Kim and Nelson|https://users.iems.northwestern.edu/~nelsonb/Publications/KimNelsonKN.pdf]
and [Birattari et al.|https://www.metaheuristics.org/downloads/BirStuPaqVar2002_gecco.pdf].

> Iterated racing

Iterated racing searches a configuration domain. It runs repeated Friedman
races with fresh scenarios, carries the winner forward and challenges it
with newly generated configurations. The same global replication cap
covers all stages and their pilot blocks.

> Known mean benchmark

Five synthetic choices have known means. All five methods use seeds 1, 7,
42 and 123. Iterated racing generates configurations from a categorical
parameter with those five choices. OCBA gives each replication a fresh seed. The racing methods
share a seed within each block, so the common offset cancels in paired
differences. The evaluation axis includes the pilot and all replications.
Early stopping is reflected in the table's Used column. Each plotted
budget is a separate run.

```{cpp, id=simulation-racing, cache=yes, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <array>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <random>
#include <stdexcept>

int main() {
    namespace o = dm::optim;
    constexpr std::array means{0.27, 0.30, 0.45, 0.55, 0.72};
    constexpr std::array<std::uint64_t, 4> seeds{1, 7, 42, 123};
    const std::vector<double> allowances{20, 40, 80, 160, 320};
    const std::vector<std::string> labels{"Kim–Nelson", "OCBA", "Confidence bound", "Friedman race", "Iterated racing"};
    const std::array methods{o::SimulationSearchMethod::kim_nelson, o::SimulationSearchMethod::ocba,
                             o::SimulationSearchMethod::confidence_race, o::SimulationSearchMethod::friedman_race};
    const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGBA> colors{{30,99,168},{205,99,31},{45,138,83},{137,72,155},{91,116,130}};
    const std::vector<o::MixedParameter> domain{{o::ParameterKind::categorical, 0, 1, means.size()}};
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    std::print("| Method | Seed | Budget | Used | Selected | Regret |\n"
               "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t method = 0; method < labels.size(); ++method) {
        std::vector<double> regret(allowances.size());
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < allowances.size(); ++i) {
            for (const auto seed : seeds) {
                std::size_t calls = 0;
                auto simulate = [&](std::size_t trial, std::uint64_t seed) {
                    ++calls;
                    std::mt19937_64 rng(seed);
                    std::uniform_real_distribution<double> uniform(-0.1, 0.1);
                    const auto shared = uniform(rng);
                    std::mt19937_64 idiosyncratic(seed ^ (trial + 1) * 0x9e3779b97f4a7c15ULL);
                    return means[trial] + shared + uniform(idiosyncratic);
                };
                const auto budget = static_cast<std::size_t>(allowances[i]);
                std::size_t selected, evaluations;
                if (method < methods.size()) {
                    o::SimulationSearchOptions options;
                    options.seed = seed;
                    options.evaluations = budget;
                    options.method = methods[method];
                    options.indifference = 0.02;
                    const auto result = o::simulation_search(simulate, means.size(), options);
                    if (!result.selected) throw std::runtime_error("No selected candidate");
                    selected = *result.selected;
                    evaluations = result.evaluations;
                } else {
                    const auto result = o::iterated_racing([&](const auto& point, std::uint64_t block_seed) {
                        return simulate(std::get<std::size_t>(point[0]), block_seed);
                    }, domain, {budget, seed, 5, 25});
                    selected = std::get<std::size_t>(result.point[0]);
                    evaluations = result.evaluations;
                }
                if (evaluations != calls || calls > budget) throw std::runtime_error("Invalid replication count");
                const auto gap = means.at(selected) - means.front();
                regret[i] += gap / seeds.size();
                std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.4f} |\n", labels[method], seed,
                           budget, calls, selected, gap);
            }
        }
        plot.line(allowances, regret, labels[method], colors[method]);
    }
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
    plot.title("Regret of the selected candidate").x_label("Replication budget")
        .y_label("Mean excess expected loss").legend(labels, colors).size(850, 470)
        .save_svg("build/simulation_racing.svg");
    std::filesystem::copy_file("build/simulation_racing.svg", "figures/simulation_racing.svg",
                               std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
```
